\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Robustness of the compression knob. For each objective we sweep $\beta \in \{10^{-4},10^{-3},10^{-2},10^{-1},1,10\}$ and report the \emph  {worst} test score any $\beta $ produces, as a deficit (in points) against the deterministic backbone of the same row; negative means the objective never falls below its backbone. Units as in Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:main}. FGIB is shown twice: at the anchor scale selected on validation in Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:main}, and at a single globally fixed anchor scale $a=16$ (a post-hoc sensitivity control, not selected a priori). Lower is better; best per rowin bold. The summary rows take medians over the 12 settings and count settings where the worst case falls more than 5 points below the backbone. The ``best $\beta $'' gain row is the maximum over the grid of the \emph  {test} score --- an exploratory upper bound, not a model-selection result; the validation-selected gain row is the selection result of Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:main} expressed relative to the backbone.}}{8}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:robust}{{2}{8}{Robustness of the compression knob. For each objective we sweep $\beta \in \{10^{-4},10^{-3},10^{-2},10^{-1},1,10\}$ and report the \emph {worst} test score any $\beta $ produces, as a deficit (in points) against the deterministic backbone of the same row; negative means the objective never falls below its backbone. Units as in Table~\ref {tab:main}. FGIB is shown twice: at the anchor scale selected on validation in Table~\ref {tab:main}, and at a single globally fixed anchor scale $a=16$ (a post-hoc sensitivity control, not selected a priori). Lower is better; best per rowin bold. The summary rows take medians over the 12 settings and count settings where the worst case falls more than 5 points below the backbone. The ``best $\beta $'' gain row is the maximum over the grid of the \emph {test} score --- an exploratory upper bound, not a model-selection result; the validation-selected gain row is the selection result of Table~\ref {tab:main} expressed relative to the backbone}{table.2}{}}
