\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The anchor scale controls the fully compressed corner. Test score of FGIB at the strongest compression pressure in the grid ($\beta =10$), as the anchor scale $a$ varies; $\Delta $ is the gap from the deterministic backbone at the largest anchor ($a{=}16$). Units as in Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:main}. At small $a$ the anchors approach the single origin of a VIB prior and the model collapses to the trivial predictor (Remark\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {rem:a0}); growing $a$ recovers the backbone, and the 100-class task needs the largest $a$, as the $\qopname  \relax o{ln}(1+(K-1)e^{-ca})$ corner value predicts.}}{32}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:anchor}{{3}{32}{The anchor scale controls the fully compressed corner. Test score of FGIB at the strongest compression pressure in the grid ($\beta =10$), as the anchor scale $a$ varies; $\Delta $ is the gap from the deterministic backbone at the largest anchor ($a{=}16$). Units as in Table~\ref {tab:main}. At small $a$ the anchors approach the single origin of a VIB prior and the model collapses to the trivial predictor (Remark~\ref {rem:a0}); growing $a$ recovers the backbone, and the 100-class task needs the largest $a$, as the $\ln (1+(K-1)e^{-ca})$ corner value predicts}{table.3}{}}
